{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtMgBeuKHf6K5QmYjFf2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The second publish failed because `similarity()` returns a Python float, and that float reached `put_item` once the table held a story. DynamoDB rejects floats. The first publish worked because an empty table produces no scores. I fixed it by converting floats to `Decimal` at the write boundary, so every path is covered, not only the one that failed. The full write-up is in `ANSWER.md`.\n\n- **Cause:** `similar[].score` is a float from `round(..., 4)`. It is only written when the table already has a story to compare against.\n- **Fix:** `src/app.py` gains `to_dynamo()`, which recursively converts floats to `Decimal(str(value))`. `publish()` calls it before `put_item`. Scores keep their 0–1 meaning.\n- **Tests:** `tests/test_publish.py` gained four tests. Three write-path tests seed the table with a story first, and one tests the converter directly. Before the fix, the write-path tests failed with the same TypeError. Now all five tests pass with `python3 -m unittest discover tests`.\n\nParts of the colleague's note I used: the diagnosis, and seeding the table in write-path tests. I did not switch scores to integer percentages. That changes what the stored value means, and the README and readers would have to change with it. `Decimal` fixes the error without that change.\n\nNothing was deployed, published or sent anywhere. The changes are uncommitted in the working tree. The records that failed were never written, so there is no float data in the table to clean up."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1490,"cache_read_input_tokens":31606,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1490},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"inp